# {{.Name}}

A Sora routing extension (contributes routing rules).

> **Status: contract v0 (proposed).** The manifest side is real - `sora-ext
> validate` accepts it and the app parses it - but core-side merging of
> contributed rules is not implemented yet. `rules.json` below is the
> proposed format the core will consume.

## Contract v0

- `rules.json` - `rules`: evaluated top-down, first match wins.
  - `match`: `domain_suffix` (matches the domain and subdomains) and/or
    `ip_cidr` (e.g. `10.0.0.0/8`).
  - `action`: `proxy` (through the VPN), `direct` (bypass), `block`.
  - `comment`: shown in the app next to the rule.
- Anything not matched falls through to the user's own rules. Contributed
  rules never silently override an explicit user rule.

## Develop / ship

```sh
sora-ext validate
sora-ext pack . -o {{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext sign --key .sora/author.key {{.ID}}.soraext
```

The `routing.rules` permission is **dangerous**: the install prompt requires
explicit confirmation, and updates that add it re-prompt the user.
